From fd4148cc44f0f77adb31d560670b184bd874a05d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guillermo Vega <guillermo.vega@balena.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:49:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] clk: rockchip: rk3399: Add more PLL rates for common pixel
 clocks

The RK3399 PLL rate table only has nine rates below 300 MHz. Since
commit d13b10ec6696 ("drm/rockchip: dw_hdmi: discard modes with
unachievable pixelclocks") dw_hdmi-rockchip rejects any HDMI mode whose
pixel clock VPLL cannot produce within 0.1%, so displays whose native
mode uses one of the missing rates fall back to a lower mode.

Add integer-mode settings for these pixel clocks:

  268.5   MHz: 2560x1600@60 (DMT, reduced blanking)
  241.5   MHz: 2560x1440@60 (CVT, reduced blanking)
  198     MHz: 2560x1080@60 (CEA VIC 90)
  185.625 MHz: 2560x1080@50 (CEA VIC 89)
  162     MHz: 1600x1200@60 (DMT)
  154     MHz: 1920x1200@60 (DMT, reduced blanking)
  146.25  MHz: 1680x1050@60 (DMT)
  138.5   MHz: 1920x1080@60 (CVT, reduced blanking)
  119     MHz: 1680x1050@60 (DMT, reduced blanking)
  108     MHz: 1280x1024@60 (DMT)
  97.75   MHz: 1600x900@60 (CVT, reduced blanking)
  88.75   MHz: 1440x900@60 (DMT, reduced blanking)
  85.5    MHz: 1366x768@60 (DMT)
  83.5    MHz: 1280x800@60 (DMT)
  81.75   MHz: 1920x540@60 (32:9 signage panels)
  71      MHz: 1280x800@60 (DMT, reduced blanking)

The VCO for all of them is between 1308 MHz and 2970 MHz, within the
800-3200 MHz range of the RK3399 PLL, and postdiv1 >= postdiv2.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Guillermo Vega <guillermo.vega@balena.io>
